@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0

# ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 - 3840x2160 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 3840x2160 instead of the stock docked 1600x900.
//
// The engine takes its size from two leaf getters, one per dock state, and
// feeds the same pair into three places: the NVN window texture plus its crop
// rectangle, the renderer's boot-time target set, and the target set that is
// rebuilt on every dock/undock. All three are moved together, and both dock
// states get the same size, so the mod holds whichever mode the game starts in.
//
// Astral Chain also ships a three-step dynamic-resolution ladder (1600x900,
// 1440x810, 1280x810 docked) that the frame pacer walks down under load. Each
// step is a set of sub-rect views into the full-size targets, so the ladder can
// only ever shrink the image. All three steps are pinned to 3840x2160, which
// both applies the new resolution and stops the game dropping below it.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 8 GiB or higher. Every render
// target, including the swap-chain textures, comes out of a fixed 310 MB
// "FrameHeap", so that heap is scaled by the 5.76x pixel ratio to 1920 MB. The app
// heap around it is nn::os::SetMemoryHeapSize(all remaining memory) and so
// follows the emulator's DRAM setting; only the FrameHeap slice is hardcoded.
//
// The FrameHeap size leaves room for the [Shadow Resolution 4096] mod. This mod
// OWNS the FrameHeap offset below; do not duplicate it in another enabled mod.

@enabled
// Display-size getters: NVN window texture size and nvnWindowSetCrop rectangle.
004328C0 08E08152   // docked width  (was 1600)
004328C8 080E8152   // docked height (was 900)
004328E0 08E08152   // handheld width  (was 1280)
004328E8 080E8152   // handheld height (was 720)
// Renderer boot: sizes the G-buffer, post-process and shadow-receive targets.
0040D5E0 08E08152   // handheld width  (was 1280)
0040D5E4 09E08152   // docked width    (was 1600)
0040D5EC 080E8152   // handheld height (was 720)
0040D5F0 090E8152   // docked height   (was 900)
// Same pair again in the dock/undock handler that recreates those targets.
0040FB00 08E08152   // handheld width  (was 1280)
0040FB04 09E08152   // docked width    (was 1600)
0040FB10 080E8152   // handheld height (was 720)
0040FB14 090E8152   // docked height   (was 900)
// Dynamic-resolution ladder, three steps. Each CSEL picked a docked or handheld
// value off the stock ladder; replacing it with an immediate pins the step.
0040F18C 01E08152   // step 0 width  (was 1600 / 1280)
0040F190 020E8152   // step 0 height (was  900 /  720)
0040F1B8 01E08152   // step 1 width  (was 1440 / 1024)
0040F1BC 020E8152   // step 1 height (was  810 /  630)
0040F1D8 01E08152   // step 2 width  (was 1280 /  800)
0040F1DC 020E8152   // step 2 height (was  810 /  630)
// Render-target heap ("FrameHeap"), was 310 MB.
0040E0B0 0800AF52   // MOVZ W8,#0x7800,LSL#16 -> 1920 MB
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_036, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
